{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_day13_decisions", "label": "Day 13 Review Follow-Up Decisions", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Review fixes, judgment calls and the encoder ideation done before Day-14 joint training, written so none of it has to be re-argued."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_quantile_crossing_post_hoc_sort", "label": "Quantile Crossing Fixed by a Post-Hoc Sort", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A plain Linear head can emit crossing quantiles, which hurts intervals but not the median; sorting at inference avoids a head-architecture change that would force a full retrain."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_granular_results_schema", "label": "Persist Granular Per-Node and Per-Origin Scores", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bootstrap CI or a paired Wilcoxon cannot be reconstructed from a mean, so per-node scores and per-origin by country sufficient statistics are persisted."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_seasonal_amplitude_limitation", "label": "Seasonal Amplitude Gap Accepted as a Limitation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zeroing sin/cos costs about 0.07 PCC, so the encoder does use seasonal phase; what is missing is last year's amplitude, which a 20-week lookback cannot reach. Feeding y[t-52] breaks the four-core-channel constraint and does nothing for Ebola, which has no year-over-year history."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_delta_target_persistence_anchor", "label": "Persistence-Anchor Delta Target (open)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Predicting the change from the last observed value needs no new channel and attacks both short-horizon persistence losses and long-horizon mean reversion, but may over-mean-revert at h10/h15 where the model currently wins."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_block_diagonal_supergraph", "label": "Block-Diagonal Joint Supergraph", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified rather than assumed: nothing in the encoder reduces over the node dimension and there is no BatchNorm, so each block's math is identical alone or inside the supergraph and no cross-block edges means no inter-dataset leakage. Locked as a permanent equivalence gate."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_per_dataset_adapters", "label": "One Shared Encoder Plus One Adapter Per Dataset", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single shared adapter fitting dengue and influenza scales would fight itself and undercut the shared-trunk claim; the trunk is the transferable asset and adapters are throwaways, which is exactly the Ebola path."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_sampler_as_loss_weights", "label": "Samplers Become Loss Weights Under Block-Diagonal Batching", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every dataset is in every batch, so a naive mean over 7,271 nodes hands dengue 98.5% of the gradient. Across-dataset and within-dengue weights compose cleanly, and per-cell country balance is used because observation density spans 97x and per-node balancing would not actually balance them."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_step_based_training", "label": "Training Defined in Steps, Not Epochs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With four datasets at a fixed per-step ratio an epoch is meaningless, since one pass over dengue is about 24 passes over japan; the cost is losing the intuitive budget and having to pick step numbers by hand."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_paired_origin_bootstrap", "label": "Paired Bootstrap Over Time Origins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resampling the same origins for both models and building the CI on the difference is what makes it robust to japan's plus or minus 7-10% seed sd; Wilcoxon across five seed-matched runs is underpowered and supporting only."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_gate_and_spatial_reads", "label": "Gate and Spatial Contribution Reads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A validation forward emits per-node mean gate and normalised spatial contribution; these are pre-head and therefore horizon-independent, and they say whether the gate-on versus g-identically-zero ablation is measuring anything."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_checkpoint_finding", "label": "No Model Weights Were Ever Saved", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "best_state was an in-memory clone discarded after the test forward, so loading existing checkpoints was impossible and derived artifacts had to be emitted during a deterministic re-run instead."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_c8_runtime_guard", "label": "C8 Runtime Ebola-Exclusion Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The guarantee had been structural only, through exclusion from the bundle list; it is now asserted at the actual selection points so any future caller trips immediately regardless of how the dataset list was built."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_p9_topo_aug_deferred", "label": "P9 Topology Augmentation Deferred", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Edge dropout and annealing do not exist, so the primary 2x2 ablation cannot run; building it would spend a day protecting a spatial channel whose value the Day-14 transfer result puts in question."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_seed_ensembling", "label": "Seed Ensembling at Inference", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five seeds are already trained, so averaging their quantiles is free variance reduction and helps most on the noisy small datasets; Ebola-safe because the few-shot adapters can be ensembled too."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_cell_pooled_vs_node_averaged", "label": "Cell-Pooled versus Node-Averaged Metric Caveat", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The saved sufficient statistics are node-pooled within each country, so the reconstructed country-macro is cell-pooled while the headline metric is node-averaged; they coincide on dense influenza panels and diverge on dengue, and an exact-headline CI would need a ~1.8 GB per-node artifact."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_day13_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_quantile_crossing_post_hoc_sort", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_day13_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_granular_results_schema", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_day13_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_seasonal_amplitude_limitation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_day13_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_day_13_delta_target_persistence_anchor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions_day_13.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pr